(3) Every woman in conditions of disability, old age, pregnancy has the right to obtain facilities and special treatment.
(4) Every elderly woman, with physical and/or mental disability, has the right to obtain care, education, training and special assistance from the Regional Government to ensure a decent life in accordance with human dignity.
(5) The Regional Government shall endeavor to establish an old age protection guarantee system for elderly women.

Article 14
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 13, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that oversee affairs of:
a. health;
b. education;
c. manpower;
d. socio-political;
e. protection and empowerment of women; and
f. peace and order;
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan with the Regional Apparatus that oversees Protection and Empowerment of Women.

Article 31
The Regional Government is responsible for:
a. implementing activities to ensure the fulfillment of women's rights;
b. providing facilities and infrastructure for the protection of women;
c. applying minimum service standards in women's protection services and the applicable standard operating procedures for repatriation and social reintegration;
d. providing implementing officers and functional officers at the UPTD

Article 26
The Implementation of Women's Empowerment in the economic field as referred to in Article 23 paragraph (2) letter c is carried out by Regional Apparatus with authority over micro, small and medium enterprises and other related agencies in the form of:
a. provision of skills and job training;
b. facilitation of the formation and strengthening of productive economic business groups;
c. facilitation of the development of marketing networks.
